# Origin

This project uses [OriginAI](https://getoriginai.com) for product design specs.

Prefer Origin MCP tools when connected; else `bunx originai` / `npx originai`.
Never raw curl. Auth: `npx originai login` → `~/.origin/settings.json` (CI: `ORIGIN_TOKEN`).

Project config: `.origin.json` (`project_id`: "2303bf76-9a83-45ca-ba34-2bf04b35de6b", `api_url`: "https://vehcxhxmmfasujqtwdat.supabase.co/functions/v1/origin-api")

## Commands (run via shell — or use MCP tools with the same names)

**Prefer MCP tools when connected. Otherwise use the `originai` CLI. NEVER
construct raw HTTP requests (curl, fetch, wget) to the API URL.**

Prefer `bunx originai` (fast) over `npx originai` (~1.2s/call).

```bash
bunx originai get-diff                                # unified diff (+/-) + to-side content
bunx originai get-diff --content-mode none            # unified diff only (no full bodies)
bunx originai sync                                    # advance release_hash after implementing
bunx originai list-documents
bunx originai list-documents --read-type workspace   # live tree (pre-release)
bunx originai get-document --id <file-id>             # only for files NOT in the diff
bunx originai grep --pattern "<regex>"
bunx originai find --file-pattern "<regex>"
bunx originai validate --content "<rpml>"   # local, no network
bunx originai create-project --name "<name>"
bunx originai write-document --name "<name>" --content "<rpml>"
bunx originai delete-document --id <file-id>
bunx originai list-proposals --status all
bunx originai describe-proposal <id> --title "…" --note "…" --rationale "…"
bunx originai submit-proposal <id>
bunx originai get-proposal-diff <id> --bind
```

**Output: all data commands print pure JSON to stdout — pipe directly into
`jq` or `json.load()` without preprocessing. Tips/status go to stderr.**

All read commands use the latest published release by default; `--read-type workspace`
reads the live tree (use when indexing a pre-release project). Token is resolved automatically.
Specs are RPML (one `.rpml` = one screen); `validate --content` before `write-document`.
Full RPML method + references: `npx originai link --skill`.

## Release badge

When the user wants a README badge (or after sync if `sync_readme_badge` is
unset): **ask yes/no** → write `"sync_readme_badge": true|false` in
`.origin.json` → on yes, insert the
`<!-- originai-release-badge:start -->…end -->` block in `README.md` using
`project_id` + `release_hash` from `.origin.json` (or `get-diff`'s `to_hash`).
URLs: `https://spec.getoriginai.com/<project_id>/<hash>/badge-dark.svg`.
Never do this silently. Full steps: see skill `Release badge` section after
`npx originai link --skill`.

## Workflow

1. If `.origin.json` has `proposal_id`, `get-diff` / `get_proposal_diff` (release <> that change request). Otherwise `get-diff` (last release vs latest). Implement from `diff` first; do **not** loop `get-document`.
2. `get-document` only for unchanged dependency files; prefer `grep`/`find`.
3. Implement code
4. `sync` → advance `release_hash` once implemented
5. **Index codebase → Origin (no release yet)**: if unbound, `create-project`
   then `npx originai link --project <id>`. Initialize **fully** in one pass.
   Write `README.rpml` first (`mode="doc"` product design doc), then
   **immediately** author one `.rpml` per page/route in its page/route
   planning — do not stop after the README. Use `validate --content` +
   `write-document --content` — no local `.rpml` files. Read back with
   `list-documents --read-type workspace` and confirm every planned page has a
   `.rpml`. Remind the user to publish a release in Origin so default reads
   can see the content.
6. **After the first release, writes stage a Change Request** (`suggested: true` is success, not an error). There is no `create_change_request` tool — the first `write-document` / MCP `write_document` creates the CR (`proposal_id` is the CR id):
1. `list-proposals --status all` (MCP `list_proposals` with `status: "all"`) — read `dismiss_reason`; do not file the same dismissed CR.
2. `validate --content` then `write-document` (MCP `write_document`). Pass `--proposal <id>` / `proposal_id` to continue; `--new-proposal` / `new_proposal: true` to start another.
3. `describe-proposal <id>` (MCP `describe_proposal`) with Issue (`title`/`note`) and Decisions + Changelog (`rationale`). Do not leave this empty.
4. `submit-proposal <id>` (MCP `submit_proposal`) when the batch is done. Never apply, dismiss, or record Ready / Not ready.
5. Tell the user to **apply** the Change Request in Origin, then **publish**. Staging is not publishing — default reads stay on the old snapshot until they publish.
6. After they publish: `get-diff` → implement → `sync`. Bind `.origin.json` `proposal_id` with `get-proposal-diff <id> --bind` **only** when this repo's next PR implements that request. Do not copy a staging id into `.origin.json` just because you wrote it.
If this repo is not linked yet after `create-project`, run `npx originai link --project <id>` so later `get-diff` / `sync` work.
